    "htmlContent": "<div class=\"facilitator-synthesis-card\">\n  <div class=\"synthesis-header\">\n    <span class=\"synthesis-badge\">導師教學梳理</span>\n    <h4 class=\"synthesis-title\">單元 00 導師地圖：啟程與開啟提問 (Opening the Question)</h4>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"synthesis-grid\">\n    <div class=\"synthesis-item\">\n      <div class=\"synthesis-item-title\">🎯 核心教學目標</div>\n      <div>破冰、建立學習契約、啟動意圖牆（Intention Wall），讓學員帶著好奇心入座。</div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"synthesis-item\">\n      <div class=\"synthesis-item-title\">💡 導師心法與節奏</div>\n      <div>不要一開始就講大道理。讓學員彼此看見、在安靜中寫下抵達狀態，體驗被接納的節奏。</div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"synthesis-item\">\n      <div class=\"synthesis-item-title\">🗣️ 關鍵話術與金句</div>\n      <div>DO/SAY: “Welcome. You are in the right room. Whatever is present for you today is welcome here.”</div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"synthesis-item\">\n      <div class=\"synthesis-item-title\">⚠️ 現場應變要點</div>\n      <div>學員剛進教室時可能帶著未接來電或緊急信件的焦慮，給予足夠的轉換留白（Spaciousness）。</div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n</div>\n<p class=\"article-paragraph\">Opening the Question</p>\n<h3 class=\"article-heading\">Arriving</h3>\n<p class=\"article-paragraph\">Ata Glance What to protect Private writing before anyvoice; thefour sets doing their ownwork; themoves named once, nottaughta round that asks no one to explain. What it builds Arrival, anhonest starting point for each person, and a shared recognition that the work matters.</p>\n<h3 class=\"article-heading\">The Journey</h3>\n<p class=\"article-paragraph\">CROSS THE THRESHOLD QUESTION SETS ONEANDTWO THE WORDS ROUND THREE AND FOUR QUESTION SETS THE INTENTION WALL (optiona)</p>\n<h3 class=\"article-heading\">EMOTIONAL ARC</h3>\n<p class=\"article-paragraph\">Quiet Inward Heard once Inward, der Lighter, andreading Short nr para tion tmtartwith Prepare th n read old e direct nd ridge ee ho om Mappnwhileoufacilitatndmak In Your Back Pocket for quick recovery.</p>\n<h3 class=\"article-heading\">Purpose</h3>\n<p class=\"article-paragraph\">Create enough quiet, permission, and orientation for people to notice what is here before thework accelerates. Emotional Agilityis named hereonce, and only as aname: thefour question setson Pages1011belongto its four moves, which are taught one module at a time. And people begin, in their ownwords, to saywhy this work matters, a shared recognition therest of the day carries.</p>\n<h3 class=\"article-heading\">What This Module Teaches</h3>\n<p class=\"article-paragraph\">Participants arrive.heynoticewhat is here, setdown what they can, and write toward four setsof questions without yet knowing what each setisfor They hear the four moves named once, as Emotional Agility, and nothing more. Bytheend they havelocated an honest starting point, and theroom has heard, in its own words, why this work matters. Let the room arrive before anything is asked of it. Name themoves once, then let the questions work. For you, the module teaches restraint: the less you explain here, the more the modules can reveal.</p>\n<h3 class=\"article-heading\">Design Notes</h3>\n<p class=\"article-paragraph\">HOLD CARRY SAVE FOR LATER What each move teaches·what the Intention “You choose what you share, and how much.&quot; The four moves, one module at a time Wall's three headingsmean·anyprogram theroom's own words for why the work matters, compassion, curiosity, courage, andvaluesin overview, biography, or agenda commentary noted, never taught back the intention s people action, each named at its module's close while people write wrote, small enough to carry authorship, at Moving On's close</p>\n<h3 class=\"article-heading\">Care</h3>\n<p class=\"article-paragraph\">something heavy, receive it, give theroom a quiet moment, and check inprivately afterward.</p>"
