    "lineCount": 22,
    "rawText": "A Hollywood script lives or dies by its“hook\":the simple premise that captures the audience's interest, sets the story in motion, and drives the action forward. Wemaynot take meetings with movie stars, buteachof us, inurwnwayacrnwritrveryminutfy day, we'rewriting the scripts that get screened at the cinema inside our heads. But in our own stories, getting hooked isn't an edge-of- your-seat thrill. lt's self-defeating reactivity: \"There's no point in trying\" \"That's the way we've always done it\" \"No one ever listens anyway” Teams and cultures e ittooilos, rigidrules, nd unexamined norms. Those well-worn “they're just resistant” lines that can crowd out ad apt ability. The film keeps running. The viewnarrows. The plot feels.. uninspired. You've seen this film before. What we think or feel starts to stand in for what is. How we act stands in for what is needed. And the scene plays again...and again. This is the cinema inside our heads. This ishooked.",
    "htmlContent": "<p class=\"article-paragraph\">A Hollywood script lives or dies by its“hook&quot;:the simple premise that captures the audience's interest, sets the story in motion, and drives the action forward. Wemaynot take meetings with movie stars, buteachof us, inurwnwayacrnwritrveryminutfy day, we'rewriting the scripts that get screened at the cinema inside our heads. But in our own stories, getting hooked isn't an edge-of- your-seat thrill. lt's self-defeating reactivity:</p>\n<blockquote class=\"article-quote\">&quot;There's no point in trying&quot;</blockquote>\n<blockquote class=\"article-quote\">&quot;That's the way we've always done it&quot;</blockquote>\n<blockquote class=\"article-quote\">&quot;No one ever listens anyway”</blockquote>\n<p class=\"article-paragraph\">Teams and cultures e ittooilos, rigidrules, nd unexamined norms. Those well-worn “they're just resistant” lines that can crowd out ad apt ability. The film keeps running. The viewnarrows. The plot feels.. uninspired. You've seen this film before. What we think or feel starts to stand in for what is. How we act stands in for what is needed. And the scene plays again...and again. This is the cinema inside our heads. This ishooked.</p>"
