    "htmlContent": "<div class=\"facilitator-synthesis-card\">\n  <div class=\"synthesis-header\">\n    <span class=\"synthesis-badge\">導師教學梳理</span>\n    <h4 class=\"synthesis-title\">單元 03 導師地圖：抽離跨出 (Stepping Out - The Room Map)</h4>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"synthesis-grid\">\n    <div class=\"synthesis-item\">\n      <div class=\"synthesis-item-title\">🎯 核心教學目標</div>\n      <div>創造刺激與回應之間的空間（The Gap），透過好奇心（Curiosity）與後設認知拉開觀照距離。</div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"synthesis-item\">\n      <div class=\"synthesis-item-title\">💡 導師心法與節奏</div>\n      <div>練習語言微調：從『我很生氣（I am angry）』轉變為『我注意到我內在有一股生氣的感受（I notice that I am feeling angry）』。看見棋局，而非淪為棋子。</div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"synthesis-item\">\n      <div class=\"synthesis-item-title\">🗣️ 關鍵話術與金句</div>\n      <div>DO/SAY: “Between stimulus and response there is a space. In that space is our power to choose our response.”</div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"synthesis-item\">\n      <div class=\"synthesis-item-title\">⚠️ 現場應變要點</div>\n      <div>抽離不是冷血逃避或解離，而是帶著溫暖的理解退後一步。注意學員是否過度理性化而切斷感受。</div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n</div>\n<p class=\"article-paragraph\">Stepping Out</p>\n<h3 class=\"article-heading\">Widening the frame</h3>\n<p class=\"article-paragraph\">Ata Glance Thechangefsaleattpningnrealomenttrougharthoonanduitrneivatsn What to protect making route, the Glass Jar line, two truths held before the“and,”and the close. Participanttratnoughacmaughttinlryuatinrytm What it bullds more of what is real becomes visible and a wiser choice becomes possible. It activates perspective and curiosity.</p>\n<h3 class=\"article-heading\">The Journey</h3>\n<p class=\"article-paragraph\">OVERVIEW EFFECT EARTH-MOON JUPITER WRITETOSEE THEGLASSJAR MOODANDTASK TWOTRUTHS QUIETCLOSE</p>\n<h3 class=\"article-heading\">EMOTIONAL ARC</h3>\n<p class=\"article-paragraph\">Curiousin the dark The view wide ns Quietand inward Playful, and capable Practical and resourced Spacious, free to choose Even wider, Short on preparation time? Startwith Pr p are then read Holds Redirects, andridges Keep The Room Mapopenwhileyoufacilitateandmark In Your Back Pocket for quick recovery.</p>\n<h3 class=\"article-heading\">Purpose</h3>\n<p class=\"article-paragraph\">Stepping Out is the ability to move out of your emotional experience your story, yourthought, or the situation you e el stuck in, soyou can observet.worry, aole, ahabit, or a group un written rule has us be or e we have noticed, and the story d ict at es the next move; from inside it we decide badly and act against what we care about. Creatinga little spacefrom a thought, emotion, role, story, situation, or system does not make themoment lessreal. It stops themoment being the whole field, so that more comes backinto view: other people, thewider context, what is also true. What thaceivesbackisagncyorrsontoughtroleratorytpruingthextmoveaartfstp all ofus. Between people, the label comes off the person: ad is agreement becomes something two people can look at together, anda concern can be said out loudwithout anyone becoming the trouble maker. In an organization, the labels are shared: weve done that before, soitwon’twork“themarketingteamjust doesn'tunderstand us, people onthebus oroffthebus. Asystem thatcan ste outside its own story finds the concern under the label and works on the risk instead oftheperson. Change is an emotional proc es, nota logical one and strategy does not create the future people do nd a to me or in a community the same distance is how apr son met uncertainty without shut t ing down. through both ne ss the holding of two truths atoncehere are many ways of stepping out a future self a ent or eyes, awalk, tm, a good question. The exercises are examples, chosen because they are small enough torunin a room and to take out ofit. What every one of them shares isthemove: change the relationship to the experience enough thatmore ofwhat is relevant in information, persectivrssibilitcanntrwingativatdnghateimassintnuactvatnit perspective and curiosity It stops there on purpose what to do with the wider view is later Emotional Agility work and it lands bet te in a room that hasfirst learned to see more before it decides, By theend, participants shouldbe able tomove a realmoment from Iam”to I notice” say what wide n ed and hold two truths inone sentence without collapsing either,</p>"
