    "rawText": "Invitation→Learning Lab Earth · Moon · Jupiter Widen the View Sometimes, to see differently, weneed to create space. We can do thisinmore than one way. The first is through language: the words we use to name an experience. We'll step through three distances: Earth, then Moon, then Jupiter. Each is a layer of awareness, frombeingin the story, to ob serving it, to seeingitn context. Notice how the same moment changes as we change vantage. Choose a recent moment when a thought, feeling, or situation had a hold on you and maybe even authored your behavior. Write a few words to label it. I am naming my hooked\"moment: Show Up Step Out Move On Walk Your Why Helpers Stepping Out from one angle...given what we knownow..right now it looks like...a working hypothesis is...one possibility i....Facts stay facts; perspective adds context. 54 @2026SUSANDAVID·Emotional Agility@·VERSION2.0",
    "htmlContent": "<p class=\"article-paragraph\">Invitation→Learning Lab Earth · Moon · Jupiter</p>\n<h3 class=\"article-heading\">Widen the View</h3>\n<p class=\"article-paragraph\">Sometimes, to see differently, weneed to create space. We can do thisinmore than one way. The first is through language: the words we use to name an experience. We'll step through three distances: Earth, then Moon, then Jupiter. Each is a layer of awareness, frombeingin the story, to ob serving it, to seeingitn context. Notice how the same moment changes as we change vantage. Choose a recent moment when a thought, feeling, or situation had a hold on you and maybe even authored your behavior. Write a few words to label it. I am naming my hooked&quot;moment:</p>\n<h3 class=\"article-heading\">Show Up</h3>\n<p class=\"article-paragraph\">Step Out Move On Walk Your Why Helpers Stepping Out from one angle...given what we knownow..right now it looks like...a working hypothesis is...one possibility i....Facts stay facts; perspective adds context.</p>"
