    "rawText": "Invitation→Two Columns We make space through language and through where and how we attend. Two Truths to Here's a third way: bothness, thecapacity to hold two truths at once. Honor Notice Think of something real in your life right now that feels complicated. A bittersweet transition. A loss that arrived alongside something good. A role that stretches you in opposite ways. Two truths can pull in opposite directions and both be real. Here are some different lenses: Me·with yourself Truth A: Excited for a new chapter Truth B: Miss what I had We·with one another Truth A: Need to confront this Truth B: Want to protect our bond Us·with the team, organization, or culture Truth A: Must adapt Truth B: Need to keep things stable Nowname afewof your own. Truth A: Truth B: Truth A: Truth B: Truth A: Truth B: STEPPING OUT 65",
