    "rawText": "Powerful Question Whatbecomes possible when you travel outside your story? Evidence Base Why This Works Stepping back from a reactive thought is linked to thinking more clearly staying ste a die r under res sure, and choosing more wisely Kross, Bruehlman-Senecal, Park, Burson, Dougherty, Shablack, Bremner, Moser &Ayduk(2014)-Usingyour own name or“you” instead of “I”while working through something stressful helped people stay calmer and clearer-headed under stress. Kross & Ayduk(20i1)—Stepping back to amore distanced view helps people make meaning from a hard experience instead of getting caught replaying it. Pennebaker & Beall (1986)—Writing about a difficult experience, both what happened and how itfelt, was linked to fewerhealth complaints in themonths that followed. Gasper & Clore(2002) —Mood shapes the scope of attention: lighter mood s open us to the big picture, heavier moods drawus toward the detail. Grossmann &Kross (2014)-People reason more wisely about others di le mm as than their own, but viewing your own situation from a distance closes the gap, makingroom to hold two truths at once. When we step out, wemake psychological space: wide enough to see, free enough to choose. Stepping Out 69",
