    "htmlContent": "<div class=\"facilitator-synthesis-card\">\n  <div class=\"synthesis-header\">\n    <span class=\"synthesis-badge\">導師教學梳理</span>\n    <h4 class=\"synthesis-title\">單元 04 導師地圖：踐行價值 (Walking Your Why - The Room Map)</h4>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"synthesis-grid\">\n    <div class=\"synthesis-item\">\n      <div class=\"synthesis-item-title\">🎯 核心教學目標</div>\n      <div>釐清個人的北極星核心價值觀（Core Values），在生命風暴中做出符合自我的勇氣抉擇。</div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"synthesis-item\">\n      <div class=\"synthesis-item-title\">💡 導師心法與節奏</div>\n      <div>Values Walk 不只是桌上分類挑選卡片，而是讓學員在身體移動中感受『為了在乎的事物而願意承受必要的不適』。</div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"synthesis-item\">\n      <div class=\"synthesis-item-title\">🗣️ 關鍵話術與金句</div>\n      <div>DO/SAY: “Courage is not the absence of fear; courage is fear walking. What is worth moving toward, even if it feels uncomfortable?”</div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"synthesis-item\">\n      <div class=\"synthesis-item-title\">⚠️ 現場應變要點</div>\n      <div>學員容易挑選『社會期待的漂亮詞彙』（如勤奮、成功），導師需挑戰：『如果沒人看見，這依然是你深層渴望活出的樣貌嗎？』</div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n</div>\n<p class=\"article-paragraph\">Walking Your Why</p>\n<h3 class=\"article-heading\">Living with everyday courage</h3>\n<p class=\"article-paragraph\">Ata Glance What to protect The WTFpage-turn (Page76),oneroute into Identifying Yourhy, the sorton Page81（goal, values, purposeprinciple),the Litmus, the Courage Lab sentence, and the close. What it builds Participants learn toread anemotion for what it points toward, tella valuefrom agoal, and takeone small step toward what matters even if fear is present. Apersonwho knows what they stand forcan actwith co here nc e when it is hard, and be centered even in the face of pressure; a team thatcan tell a values conflict from a goal conflict can reach a shared understanding; a culture wherevalues are lived is one people can trust.</p>\n<h3 class=\"article-heading\">The Journey</h3>\n<p class=\"article-paragraph\">INNER CORE WTF NOTGOALS VALUES, YOURWHY VALUES HOUSE VALUES TRAPS WORKABILITY STRESS UNDER COURAGE LAB QUIET CLOSE</p>\n<h3 class=\"article-heading\">EMOTIONAL ARC</h3>\n<p class=\"article-paragraph\">oriented Warm, Alaugh, then aquestion Clear recognition Quiet Reflective complexity Honest Cons e que nt i al, helpful Steadied the fear present Willing.with Grounded, resourced Shortonprparationtme?tartwith Prepare then read Holdsedirectsand Bridgeseep The Room Mapopenwhileyoufacilitateandmak In Your Back Pocketfor quick recovery.</p>\n<h3 class=\"article-heading\">Purpose</h3>\n<p class=\"article-paragraph\">Help participants find a sense of direction strong enough to act from when e motion, ressure, approval ha bit, anduncertaintypull.h Participant Workbook describes it thisway (Pages 7O-72):Like a gymnast with a strong core, when you have a deep inner sense of your values, youcanmovefluidly and gracefully through whatever lifebrings.“when people connect with theirvalues, they actwith coherence and selftrust, even when emotions are strongor the path i sun c learn der pressure, clear values reduce re activity</p>\n<blockquote class=\"article-quote\">“Values steady courage: they help us face discomfort and keep faith with what matters in dificult moments. And for organizations:</blockquote>\n<blockquote class=\"article-quote\">&quot;Values expression is essential to healthy leadership and psychologically safe culture.&quot;</blockquote>\n<p class=\"article-paragraph\">Walking Your Whygoeswell beyond naming values. Values matter because lifeisnot simple: a erson can knowwhat they feeland stil not knowwhat todo. Values do not remove trade off uncertainty, orcost.hey helpanswer: Who do Ichoose tobehere, andwhat direction should mynext action serve?hisiswhat moves values from a statement into daily life, athome and atwork.</p>\n<h3 class=\"article-heading\">What This Module Teaches</h3>\n<p class=\"article-paragraph\">Participants first meet an emotion of their own and askwhat it isfor: whatvalue orneed it points toward. Emotions often signal that somethingmatters.nlythendoesthemodule saywhat avalueis, andwhatit isnot: a direction not a est i nation chose not inherited something a goal serves rather than something a goal r places Identifying Your Why gives each person their own words for it, on the page or on thefloorif you run the Values Walk. The House shows thatmore than one value matters at once; Values Traps names is. Check Work ability asks what arepeated values-connected choice builds How Values Protect Us Under Stress lets a value steady a person while the difficulty is still there and he Courage Lab turns all f it into ones ma lbs e rv able action even with fear still preent. Let theroomread an e motion for its function before anyonenames a valueet a value bea direction before anyone plans. The practitioner'srole is to keep values from becoming rhetoric Keep returning to one question how does thisvalue live?</p>"
