    "rawText": "What Can Go Wrong IF THIS HAPPENS TRYTHIS WTF turns into“this emotion always means this\" \"That's a hypothesis. What might it be pointing toward for you?\" People choose impressive values or police others Move out of should. \"My values conflict”makes the choice impossible Takethem to Page 80 andrun itsmove: name both values, choosea principle that honors each, sequence the goals. Values House becomes a balance scorecard Return to the pages words ro or ms you move between, a quiet room still waitingfor yourreturn; attention, not balance. Avalue becomes identity oravoidance Askwhat truly living the value would look likerather than pro v ing or defendingit. Organizational values become compliance language Look for where thevalues truly overlap, where a value of the person’s might show up inside the organization’s; where they show up in behavior, and where they don't; no one has to adopt a value toprove commitment. Workabilitybecomes\"whateverworks\" Bring back Page88's three tests: toward or away, the100-times test, time and people lens. Values are used tomake harmful work tolerable Sayit plainly: avalue gives direction insideahard situation; itisnota reason to accept one that is harming you or the people around you. Courage becomes pushing harder Courage is willing ne ss tomove toward what matters, not themost dis comfort a person can bear, andnever gratuitous discomfort. How You'll Know It Landed STRONG SIGNALS NEAR-MISSES Someone catches a should in their own value selection·an emotion A beautiful values list completed likea form·values used to justify becomes a question rather than an instruction·“my values conflict” rigidity.courage equated with suffering becomesmy goals conflict”·a participant names the cost of a choice without treating cost as failure·workability enters ordinary conversation the Courage Lab produces small observable actions· someone can say， ineffect,“I can feel this and still knowhow I want to act” EMOTIONALAGILITYPRACTITIONERGUIDE Walking Your Why·PRACTITIONER11",
    "htmlContent": "<p class=\"article-paragraph\">What Can Go Wrong</p>\n<h3 class=\"article-heading\">IF THIS HAPPENS TRYTHIS</h3>\n<p class=\"article-paragraph\">WTF turns into“this emotion always means this&quot; &quot;That's a hypothesis. What might it be pointing toward for you?&quot; People choose impressive values or police others Move out of should. &quot;My values conflict”makes the choice impossible Takethem to Page 80 andrun itsmove: name both values, choosea principle that honors each, sequence the goals. Values House becomes a balance scorecard Return to the pages words ro or ms you move between, a quiet room still waitingfor yourreturn; attention, not balance. Avalue becomes identity oravoidance Askwhat truly living the value would look likerather than pro v ing or defendingit. Organizational values become compliance language Look for where thevalues truly overlap, where a value of the person’s might show up inside the organization’s; where they show up in behavior, and where they don't; no one has to adopt a value toprove commitment. Workabilitybecomes&quot;whateverworks&quot; Bring back Page88's three tests: toward or away, the100-times test, time and people lens. Values are used tomake harmful work tolerable Sayit plainly: avalue gives direction insideahard situation; itisnota reason to accept one that is harming you or the people around you. Courage becomes pushing harder Courage is willing ne ss tomove toward what matters, not themost dis comfort a person can bear, andnever gratuitous discomfort.</p>\n<h3 class=\"article-heading\">How You'll Know It Landed</h3>\n<p class=\"article-paragraph\">STRONG SIGNALS NEAR-MISSES Someone catches a should in their own value selection·an emotion A beautiful values list completed likea form·values used to justify becomes a question rather than an instruction·“my values conflict” rigidity.courage equated with suffering becomesmy goals conflict”·a participant names the cost of a choice without treating cost as failure·workability enters ordinary conversation the Courage Lab produces small observable actions· someone can say， ineffect,“I can feel this and still knowhow I want to act”</p>"
