    "lineCount": 16,
    "rawText": "Invitation→Prompt One of the beautiful things about values is that they aren't rigid rules or Build Your narrow lanes. They give us an inner architecture that supports us rather than confines us. Values House You can think of your values as rooms in a house. You movebetween them, sometimes lingering, sometimes passing through quickly. Evenwhenyou're not ina particular room, it still exists, waiting for your return. Spending time in one space doesn't mean you've stopped caring about the others. Working late doesn't erase your love of adventure. Caring for family doesn't negate your need for independence. Whatmattersisn't constant balance, but the ability to notice where you are, where you have nt been in aw hi land what might be calling for our attention next. RELATIONSHIPS RESPONSIBILITY CHALLENGE AUTO NOMy COMMUNITY GENER OSITY ERS DIV ity ADVENTURE TRVST HONESTY Walking Your Why 83",
