    "rawText": "Evidence Base Why This Works Reflecting on personal values is associated with reduced neural stress responses and sustained self-management under pressure. Dutcher, Eisenberger, Woo, Klein, Harris, Levine&Creswell (2020) —Reflecting on personal values activated reward-related brain regions and reduced activity in threat-related regions duringa stress f ul task. ·Schmeichel &Vohs(2009)—Affirming core values restored self- management after sustained effort. When we walk our why, what we value becomes howwe live. Howwe live becomes the cultures we help create. 93 Walking Your Why",
