    "lineCount": 11,
    "rawText": "DISCOMf ORT Invitation→Prompt The Teeter-Totter Principle invites you tofind the balance point between The Teeter- these two extremes — the spot where your competence and comfort meet the Totter Principle excitement (and even healthy stress) of the unknown. We have a word for too little(underwhelmed) and a word for too much(overwhelmed),and almost never use the onebetween them: whelmed. This is the zone where learning becomes alive again, where you operate at the edge of your ability: otbored, notoverwhelmedbutngagedinacreativ tension that stretches you just enough to grow. It is intentional, a placeyou choose andkeep choosing. Moving On 109",
    "htmlContent": "<p class=\"article-paragraph\">DISCOMf ORT</p>\n<h3 class=\"article-heading\">Invitation→Prompt</h3>\n<p class=\"article-paragraph\">The Teeter-Totter Principle invites you tofind the balance point between The Teeter- these two extremes — the spot where your competence and comfort meet the Totter Principle excitement (and even healthy stress) of the unknown. We have a word for too little(underwhelmed) and a word for too much(overwhelmed),and almost never use the onebetween them: whelmed. This is the zone where learning becomes alive again, where you operate at the edge of your ability: otbored, notoverwhelmedbutngagedinacreativ tension that stretches you just enough to grow. It is intentional, a placeyou choose andkeep choosing.</p>\n<h3 class=\"article-heading\">Moving On 109</h3>"
